---
permalink: "/sitemap.xml"
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
---
{#- The XML sitemap robots.txt has been pointing at. No layout: this is not an
    HTML page, so it must not pick up base.njk.

    The URL list lives in the sitemapUrls collection (eleventy.config.js) rather
    than here, so that what robots.txt advertises and what /sitemap/ shows are
    derived from the same records instead of two hand-kept lists. That is the
    failure the human sitemap page was already fixed for.

    lastmod is omitted per-URL where the record has no date_modified — an absent
    lastmod is valid and honest; a fabricated one is worse than none. -#}
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<urlset xmlns="http://www.sitemaps.org/schemas/sitemap/0.9">
{%- for entry in collections.sitemapUrls %}
	<url>
		<loc>{{ global.site_url }}{{ entry.url }}</loc>
		{%- if entry.lastmod %}
		<lastmod>{{ entry.lastmod | isoDate }}</lastmod>
		{%- endif %}
	</url>
{%- endfor %}
</urlset>
